  "plain": "In 1947 something came down near Roswell, New Mexico, and it was later explained away as a balloon. The point of this story is that the men at Roswell were hardly people who would mistake a balloon for a flying saucer. Bryce Zabel, a guest on an episode about Hollywood and UFOs, says without naming a source that the people at Roswell were \"the only people running a nuclear bomber base in the world in 1947.\" Michels makes the same point himself, a little differently: Roswell \"wasn't a random desert,\" he says, but \"the largest concentration of nuclear weapons in the world at the time.\" Both tell it because if those men really couldn't tell a saucer from a balloon, that would be hard to believe."
}
